## an interval
let card = import("data/card.csv")
let iv = card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + expersq + black + south + smsa + educ, instruments: educ ~ nearc4 + nearc2)
iv.ar_test()

---
ar_test · iv · educ
  H0: the coefficient of educ is zero          β = 0
  H1: the coefficient of educ is not zero      β ≠ 0
F(2, 3,002) = 7.16   p = 0.001
decision at α = 0.05: reject H0 (p = 0.001)
95% confidence set for the coefficient of educ: from 0.0863 to 0.3166
Anderson–Rubin test on the instruments nearc4, nearc2; valid however weak the instruments
note: data/card.csv read as CSV: 3,010 rows × 35 variables, types guessed; CSV carries no labels, value labels or categories (line 1)
warning[W1007]: weak instruments: the Cragg–Donald F is 9.45, under 10 (line 2)
  = help: with weak instruments the estimate leans towards the least-squares one and its confidence interval is too narrow; `ar_test()` gives a test and a confidence set that hold however weak the instruments are

